 ritual meal on the other [SUPPORTED: https://www.mithraeum.eu/monument/259]; The relief is two-sided [SUPPORTED: https://mithras.tertullian.org/display.php?page=cimrm1896]; One side shows a bull slain [SUPPORTED: https://mithras.tertullian.org/display.php?page=cimrm1896]; The other side shows a ritual meal [SUPPORTED: https://mithras.tertullian.org/display.php?page=cimrm1896]; The carving is of gray limestone [SUPPORTED: https://mithras.tertullian.org/display.php?page=cimrm1896]; The carving comes from a temple of Mithra [SUPPORTED: https://marjanhajnal.wordpress.com/2014/02/01/hram-boga-mitre-u-konjicu-kult-boga-mithrasa-znacaj-i-karakteristike-mirjana-kapetanovic/]; Mithra, to whom the temple was dedicated, is the sun god [SUPPORTED: https://mithras.tertullian.org/display.php?page=cimrm1896]; The temple is atypical for its floor at ground level [SUPPORTED: https://marjanhajnal.wordpress.com/2014/02/01/hram-boga-mitre-u-konjicu-kult-boga-mithrasa-znacaj-i-karakteristike-mirjana-kapetanovic/]"}]'::jsonb),
